# Compensation & Benefits

## Overview

Compensation and Benefits covers how an organization designs, manages and reviews employee pay and benefits.

The HRBP helps ensure that compensation practices support business needs, employee retention, fairness and organizational performance.

---

## Key Areas

- Compensation strategy
- Salary structure
- Pay benchmarking
- Salary review
- Benefits administration
- Allowances
- Incentives and bonuses
- Payroll coordination
- Compensation analysis
- Internal pay equity
- Total rewards
- Employee communication

---

## HRBP Responsibilities

The HRBP supports management by:

- Reviewing compensation trends
- Supporting salary reviews
- Identifying pay-related concerns
- Supporting workforce budgeting
- Reviewing benefits effectiveness
- Advising managers on compensation matters
- Supporting internal equity reviews
- Monitoring compensation-related employee issues

---

## Key Compensation Metrics

- Average salary
- Salary range
- Compa-ratio
- Salary increase percentage
- Payroll cost
- Benefits cost
- Compensation cost per employee
- Internal pay equity
- Employee turnover related to compensation

---

## Total Rewards

Total rewards may include:

- Basic salary
- Allowances
- Bonuses
- Incentives
- Health benefits
- Leave benefits
- Retirement benefits
- Learning and development
- Recognition
- Career development
- Flexible work arrangements

---

## Governance

Compensation decisions should be guided by:

- Company policy
- Employment contracts
- Applicable employment laws
- Internal salary structures
- Approved budgets
- Market information
- Organizational needs

---

## Confidentiality

No confidential employee salary information or personally identifiable employee data should be uploaded to this portfolio.

Examples and datasets should be fictionalized or anonymized.

